  "observations": [
    "The regulator and four capacitors are on the front. Input/output/delay routes enter their adjacent pins directly; output-capacitor ground returns to pin 4 and the exposed pad.",
    "The back-side feedback and trim network has no crossing; its output-sense branch passes to the left of the feedback via and the neighboring C205 body.",
    "The auxiliary bypass connection follows the corridor between C106 and N_R75; the return runs above it. Native clearance checks report no violations.",
    "The new In4 enable link is local to U102. All five added vias are outside the existing U20 planes; native refill and the independent audit preserve all four earlier zone outlines and polygons.",
    "The front input ground reaches the exposed pad on the right side of the regulator; ground regions, thermal stitching, PG and wider supply distribution are still incomplete.",
    "Full-board views retain extensive unrouted circuitry. This review does not establish electrical performance or fabrication readiness."
  ],
